tags[1]: sdk-capabilities
created_at: "2026-06-02T07:26:44.539Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T23:25:00.118Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T23:25:00.117Z"
author: codex
release: 2026.6.2
resolution: "Work completed and released in 2026.6.2. Release attribution verified by containment rather than by date: git merge-base --is-ancestor 175725a v2026.06.02 succeeds, so 2026.6.2 is the first release whose tree holds the implementing commit. An earlier revision of this record said 2026.6.2-1; that came from matching the item's last-activity DATE to a release and is superseded."
expected_result: "A closed item whose changelog entry appears under the 2026.6.2 heading, the first release actually containing 175725a, leaving the current release notes untouched."
actual_result: "Before this closeout the item had remained in_progress with no activity since its work shipped, so the delivery was missing from the changelog while still being counted as open work in every fleet audit. Closing it with an explicit release attribution is what added the historical entry."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T23:17:12.354Z",claude-code,"Release attribution corrected to 2026.6.2 after review. The first attribution used the item's last-activity DATE, which is unsound: an item can be touched before the release that finally carried its code. Verified instead by tag containment — git tag --contains 175725a reports 2026.6.2 as the first release holding the implementation commit. Greptile caught this on PR #67 by noticing a historical release predating its implementation."
close_reason: "Retired as shipped: the kanban board and full-text search data endpoints was completed and released in 2026.6.2, verified by tag containment against implementing commit 175725a. The item was never closed and sat in progress ever since, inflating every fleet audit."
body: ""
